WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.837
Views can help separate source data from analytical representation.

00:00:04.837 --> 00:00:07.807
The raw table preserves provenance.

00:00:07.807 --> 00:00:11.437
A clean view applies standardized transformations.

00:00:11.437 --> 00:00:15.507
A quality view exposes rows that need review.

00:00:15.507 --> 00:00:22.732
Downstream analysis can use the prepared layer without permanently overwriting the source.

00:00:22.732 --> 00:00:25.517
This also makes the cleaning logic visible in SQL.

00:00:25.517 --> 00:00:34.597
A quarantine pattern separates questionable records from trusted analytical output without deleting evidence.

00:00:34.597 --> 00:00:43.667
Views are useful for reusable cleaning logic because they let you expose a consistent cleaned representation

00:00:43.667 --> 00:00:46.482
while keeping raw source data intact.

00:00:46.482 --> 00:00:49.680
That improves reproducibility and auditability.
